1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Every P2P crypto deal has a trust paradox:
pay upfront and risk getting scammed,

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,500
deliver work first and risk getting ghosted,
or use centralized escrow with custody risk.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Meet SafeDeal — non-custodial P2P escrow on Avalanche.
Smart contracts hold the funds, RFC 8785 locks the terms.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Flow 1: Cooperative Trade.
The seller drafts deal terms and computes an RFC 8785 hash.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Both TypeScript and our Rust backend produce the exact
termsHash, anchored on Avalanche Fuji via createTrade.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The buyer funds the escrow, the seller marks delivery,
and the buyer approves and releases payment on-chain.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
SafeDeal uses Pull-Payment withdraw() instead of inline pushes,
preventing reentrancy and reverting-recipient DoS attacks.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The seller claims their AVAX directly from the contract.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Flow 2: Open-Buyer & Refund Protection.
Leave the buyer blank to create a shareable payment link.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The first wallet to call fundTrade locks in as the buyer.
If delivery misses the deadline, or the seller refunds,

11
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:45,000
the buyer reclaims 100% of their AVAX directly on-chain
without needing permission from any admin.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Flow 3: Dispute & 2-of-3 Consensus.
Participants upload private evidence verified by magic-bytes.

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:10,000
SIWE authentication and role checks enforce strict 403
isolation so outsiders can never view dispute files.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Unlike god-mode arbiters, SafeDeal requires 2-of-3 matching
votes across Buyer, Seller, and Arbiter to settle.

15
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:40,000
And if anyone ghosts, a 14-day timeout fallback unlocks
a deterministic 50/50 split so funds are never trapped.

16
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Built with Foundry invariant fuzzing, a Clean Architecture
Rust backend on Railway, and a reload-safe React UI.

17
00:02:51,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Live now on Avalanche Fuji Testnet at avalanche-9b099.web.app.
